{{={= =}=}}
{
  {=!
    These are the `bundle` and `start` scripts from `package.json`, run directly instead of through
    `npm run`, which would start a shell and npm several times on every restart.
    nodemon stops for good if the command exits with code 2 right after starting (it assumes the
    command has a syntax error), and `tsc` uses that code for type errors, so `|| exit 1` makes it
    wait for file changes instead.
  =}
  "exec": "tsc --build && rollup --config --silent && node --enable-source-maps -r dotenv/config bundle/server.js || exit 1",
  "env": {
    "NODE_ENV": "development"
  },
  "watch": [
    "src/",
    "{= relativeUserSrcDirPath =}",
    ".env"
  ],
  "comment-filip": "We now have to watch {= relativeUserSrcDirPath =} because we're importing client files directly",
  "ext": "ts,mts,js,mjs,json",
  {=!
    nodemon handles two different kinds of POSIX signals:
    a. Which signal is sent to the child process when an update occurs.
    b. Which signal we can send nodemon to trigger a manual restart.

    The `signal` option here specifies (a), but nodemon internally also uses it
    to choose (b): If (a) is on its default value of SIGUSR2, nodemon will use
    SIGHUP for (b), or SIGUSR2 otherwise.

    We don't want nodemon to react to terminal closing (SIGHUP) as a reload, and
    instead want it to terminate. That's why we're changing the signal off its
    default.
  =}
  "signal": "SIGTERM"
}
